{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>On the seventh day.</b> Some say they offered on the Sabbath, and it was a temporary ruling. Others say that it is the seventh day of the dedication of the altar. Those who object say that the beginning of the dedication was not the first day of the week, but this does not help, for it is impossible that there not be a Sabbath among twelve days. The correct view in my eyes is that it is like the second interpretation. \"Slaughter of peace offerings,\" and likewise \"on the seventh day\" in the encircling of Jericho, and likewise the seven days of the dedication of the Temple, on account of the day of affliction of the soul."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:43.891773364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}